WEBVTT

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:12.980
Where am I?

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.840
No movement on board station Nakhodka.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.710
Recon rocket will arrive in ten minutes.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.190
The Leto orbital laser has activated.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:39.100
No...

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:42.680
Leto is retargeting. Image on screen.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.860
So Leto has fallen into Vesna's hands?

00:00:56.690 --> 00:01:00.120
Probably not just Leto,
but Osen and Zima, as well.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:02.580
So we won't be able to

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:05.190
handle this situation 
on our own anymore...

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.370
Send a request for help 
to the military...

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.400
Leto's retargeting.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.640
It's targeting...

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:15.550
Leto is on the other side 
of the Earth currently,

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:19.510
but in three hours, it will be in a 
position to attack our nation.

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:22.910
So, even if we asked for help...

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:24.020
It'd be too late.

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:29.770
Do we just have to sit and watch as 
our nation is burned to the ground?

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:32.080
What is this?

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:35.150
What idiot is talking?

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:38.190
It seems to be a transmission from Nakhodka.

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:40.010
Nakhodka?

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:42.870
I thought it was taken over 
and currently unmanned.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.120
It should be, but...

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:50.240
I can hear a voice.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:51.670
Are you inside?

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:56.040
We're not inside, 
but we can see you through it.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:58.680
You can see me?

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:01.520
I'm Takeda Shingen.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:04.470
Some people call me the Cavalry Queen.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.480
Which means she's...

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:10.570
A warring states general?!

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:45.390
I see.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:46.920
I think I get it.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:51.020
So a lot of people besides 
me have come to this world.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:53.610
We've never heard of a General arriving

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.650
on a space station before, though.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:04:01.320
So in my case, I came here 
to Nakhodka, not Earth.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:04.180
You were lucky though, Devushka Takeda.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:06.920
If you'd gone outside Nakhodka...

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:08.920
a person can only survive the emptiness

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:11.480
of space for about 15 seconds.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:16.480
So I might've died as 
soon as I got here.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.440
So, Devushka Takeda.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.140
Would you like to make a deal with us?

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:25.390
If I agree, do I then get to go to Earth?

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:27.790
We'd like you to neutralize Vesna 9000,

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:30.370
the artificial intelligence 
that operates Nakhodka.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.230
Artificial intelligence?

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:34.700
A machine with the power to think.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:40.340
Vesna 9000 used guard-roids 
to take over Nakhodka.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:45.030
We'd like you to figure out a way 
past them and stop Vesna.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:48.800
Then isn't it hearing us now?

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:53.070
For now, it will be analyzing 
the threat, not acting.

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:54.210
While it's distracted with that...

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.930
I can go stop it.

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:58.190
I think I can do that.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:01.110
Then you'll need to find 
a support droid first.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.570
Support droid?

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:13.240
Fasad 29.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:15.000
It's an older model,

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.330
but that means it should be 
immune to Vesna's control.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.540
Him?

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:22.010
He'll help you.

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:23.420
I hope so.

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:25.950
Good morning, Mikhail.

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:29.070
You've come to awaken 
me as promised, yes?

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:30.120
Excuse me.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:31.420
I seem to have the wrong person.

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:32.720
Not at all.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:35.330
By the way, I'm Takeda Shingen.

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:37.560
Call me Shingen.

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:42.350
It seems many years have 
passed while I was asleep.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:46.930
But Mikhail didn't come 
to wake me up, it seems.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:49.900
He was busy, I'm sure.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:51.820
He isn't the kind of person who

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:53.460
would forget a promise.

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:56.470
Thus, if he did not keep his promise,

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:59.500
there must have been 
some reason he couldn't.

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:01.340
In other words?

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:04.790
He must have died.

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:06.300
He died?

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:09.470
Then I guess he couldn't 
come to wake you up.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:11.250
But he promised.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:14.710
He promised he'd come to wake me up.

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:17.050
Um, are you upset?

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:18.140
Yes. Very.

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:22.950
I like you.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:26.670
Hey, Fasad, would you help me?

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:29.320
My partner is Mikhail, and only him.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:32.060
That's some splendid loyalty.

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:34.160
You hear me?

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.750
I'll explain things to 
him and get him to help.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:37.660
Thanks.

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:44.670
So that's why we've 
reactivated you, Fasad 29.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:47.390
I see. I understand the situation.

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:48.820
If the motherland is in danger,

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:50.440
I must rise to the occasion.

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:52.970
However, my calculations indicate

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:54.990
that it is improbable for a 
lone woman to defeat

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:57.530
Vesna-9000 and the guard-roids.

00:06:57.530 --> 00:06:59.360
I'm not alone.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:00.880
I have you.

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:03.190
I will be of no help in battle.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:06.910
I can make tea, though.

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:09.440
If you can calculate, that's enough.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:11.950
Leave the fighting to me.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:15.700
There are too many of them 
for one person to handle.

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:17.830
Or did that concept not 
exist in your world?

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:19.790
Then let me ask you this, Fasad.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:23.950
Have you never heard the 
phrase "ikki-tousen"?

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:26.060
A warrior worth a thousand.

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:29.720
By the way, they used to 
call me the Cavalry Queen.

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:29.720
<b>Cavalry Queen</b>

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:33.340
Indeed, there probably 
aren't a thousand of them.

00:07:33.670 --> 00:07:37.250
But they are more powerful than a human.

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:38.770
And...

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:43.520
Must be a patrol.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:45.440
What are you going to do, Shingen?

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:52.400
As fast as the wind.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:55.000
Takeda Style Jiu-Jitsu, Wind Attack.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:56.780
Pretty sharp, don't you think?

00:07:56.780 --> 00:08:00.150
I totally broke them.

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:02.570
They're a lot weaker than I thought.

00:08:02.570 --> 00:08:05.600
Your combat skills far 
exceed that of a human.

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:07.840
Who are you?

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:09.560
Didn't I tell you?

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:12.150
Takeda Shingen, the Cavalry Queen.

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:17.300
You spoke of a Wind Attack just now.

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:26.210
<b>"Fast as the wind, 
Quiet as the forest, 
Daring as fire, 
Immovable 
as the mountain."</b>

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:18.800
Sun Tzu, yes?

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:20.270
You're pretty smart.

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:22.380
That's right, I took it from him.

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:26.230
You seem better informed 
than I imagined.

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:29.680
I'm good at most things, except math.

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:37.740
The Cavalry Queen, Takeda Shingen.

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:40.720
Why is a human still on board Nakhodka?

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:42.420
Evaluating necessity of elimination.

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:44.330
Evaluating necessity of elimination.

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:47.880
What's this?

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:49.980
An AK-74.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:51.590
The '74 model.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:55.590
It's an old weapon now, 
but a very reliable gun.

00:08:56.290 --> 00:09:00.300
Many wonderful things were 
made in '74, Shingen.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:04.050
What kinds of things?

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:08.230
The first Fasad was made in '74.

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:11.160
Well, that's good enough for me.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:16.030
Pretty powerful.

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:17.480
Be careful.

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:19.560
It's very loud.

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:21.410
I guess so.

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:23.060
So is this the right way?

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:24.350
I believe so.

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:25.600
Be careful.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:28.790
As you get closer to the station's center,

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:31.800
you'll cease to feel any weight.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:37.180
It's kind of unsettling 
to float like this.

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:40.780
Devushka Takeda, what's the situation?

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:43.510
It's been an hour.

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:47.230
I defeated five advance guard-roids.

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:50.450
I estimate, after that, 
that I could take on 50 at once.

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:53.890
And I have this AK-74 thing, too.

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:57.900
Devushka Takeda, you're not authorized 
to use weapons on the station.

00:09:57.900 --> 00:10:01.010
Oh my, you seem to be breaking up.

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:02.700
I'll hang up.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.830
Shingen, my sensors couldn't

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.370
detect any problems with the headset.

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:11.100
Is something wrong?

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:13.340
It looks like there was something else

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.590
you should've been detecting.

00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:17.670
My apologies.

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:19.380
I was busy listening to

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:21.240
the conversation between you and control.

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:23.600
Well, I'm sure they would've 
found us eventually.

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:27.230
The sound reflects.

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:29.830
Huh?

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:33.360
So they've adapted to the AK-74.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:35.610
Shingen, you should use that 
technique from earlier.

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:40.200
Okay, now I'll use the Forest Attack.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:38.650
<b>Forest</b>

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:39.740
<b>Wind</b>

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:39.740
<b>Fire</b>

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:39.740
<b>Mountain</b>

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:39.530
<b>Forest</b>

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:39.740
<b>Forest</b>

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:42.280
<b>Forest</b>

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:43.620
<b>Forest</b>

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:44.910
<b>Forest</b>

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:44.910
<b>Forest</b>

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:45.240
<b>Forest</b>

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:45.740
<b>Forest</b>

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:46.250
<b>Forest</b>

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:46.910
<b>Forest</b>

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:46.910
<b>Forest</b>

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:46.910
<b>Forest</b>

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:51.520
As quiet as the forest.

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:54.590
Takeda Style Jiu-Jitsu, Forest Attack.

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:57.980
That attack was not very quiet at all.

00:10:57.980 --> 00:11:01.360
My sensors detected an 
excess of 100 decibels.

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:03.530
Do you mean it was loud?

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:05.930
Very loud, Shingen.

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:07.680
My!

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:10.930
Well, it all worked out. It's fine.

00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:12.060
Indeed.

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:14.940
It didn't matter whether it 
was quiet or not this time.

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:24.610
Is this a weapon, Fasad?

00:11:24.610 --> 00:11:26.010
A flamethrower.

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:28.900
As the name suggests, it throws flames.

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:30.790
It throws flames?

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.920
Shingen, I'm sure you 
know better than to—

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:39.360
As daring as fire.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:42.630
How do you like my Takeda 
Style Jiu-Jitsu, Fire Attack?

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:45.630
That is very clearly not Jiu-Jitsu, Shingen.

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:47.140
Also it's not "daring as fire."

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:48.640
It <i>is</i> fire.

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:50.990
Use what's at hand.

00:11:50.990 --> 00:11:52.480
That's Takeda Style.

00:11:55.950 --> 00:11:58.210
It's out of fuel.

00:11:58.210 --> 00:11:59.210
Oh my.

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:01.690
But we're almost to Vesna-san.

00:12:01.690 --> 00:12:02.990
Let's go.

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:06.870
It's a little too quiet.

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:11.000
Vesna-9000 should know we're coming.

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:15.130
The fact that she still 
isn't attacking means...

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:18.740
She's either out of guard-roids 
or laying an ambush.

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:20.960
This is the only path to Vesna.

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:23.190
It is clearly the latter.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:28.260
I can fight 50 of those guys at once.

00:12:28.530 --> 00:12:30.480
The risk is too great.

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:32.640
I knew that from the start.

00:12:33.090 --> 00:12:37.560
My sensors detect an enemy 
ambush beyond this point.

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:39.980
I know that, too.

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:47.610
Oh my, I didn't know there 
were so many guard-roids.

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:49.870
I am slightly surprised, as well.

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:02.220
Um...

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:04.800
We're running, Fasad.

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:06.180
Yes, Shingen.

00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:10.720
Let's head in there for now.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:13.090
There is a high possibility 
we'll be locked inside.

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:14.520
I cannot agree.

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.480
It's better than dying out here.

00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:22.390
We're safe in here for now.

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:26.570
I've detected Vesna attempting to hack the door.

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:32.310
I've locked out the signal from Vesna.

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:34.250
It is only temporary, however.

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:36.120
You're a life-saver, Fasad.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:39.430
I need you for this stuff.

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:42.370
However, we haven't solved anything.

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:44.610
Yup.

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:46.260
Fasad, what's this room?

00:13:47.370 --> 00:13:48.260
What's this?

00:13:48.610 --> 00:13:50.900
A worker pod.

00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:53.920
You can get in them and 
go outside from here.

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:56.770
Then why don't we go outside?

00:13:56.770 --> 00:14:00.690
You'll be at a disadvantage if we do.

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:03.080
There's no air out there.

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:05.270
It will restrict the number 
of actions you can take.

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:09.210
I think it'd work out.

00:14:09.210 --> 00:14:10.740
Intuition?

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:12.210
Is that not enough?

00:14:12.210 --> 00:14:15.660
It's not, but at the same 
time, it's somehow exciting.

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:21.090
When I'm with you, I 
remember Mikhail somehow.

00:14:21.370 --> 00:14:24.210
Are we alike?

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:26.850
Especially in how intuition 
guides your actions.

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:28.720
Even when I told him something correct,

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:31.520
he wouldn't listen to me at all.

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:33.910
But you liked him.

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:34.810
Yes.

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:38.690
Oh, speaking of likes, 
Mikhail loved Japanese food.

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:39.630
Oh?

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:41.670
Ever since he tried the tips of chicken wings,

00:14:41.670 --> 00:14:45.290
he wished to make it 
popular in his own country.

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:46.060
Oh my.

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:50.670
Then why don't you carry on the 
dream he couldn't fulfill?

00:14:50.670 --> 00:14:52.330
I can make them,

00:14:52.330 --> 00:14:54.460
but as I cannot eat them, 
my recommendation

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:56.350
is of little value.

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:58.390
I suppose that's true.

00:14:58.390 --> 00:15:00.900
Ready to go out?

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:03.240
I can control the pod,

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:06.780
but once I leave it, the door 
will only last 20 seconds.

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:08.360
20 seconds.

00:15:08.360 --> 00:15:10.130
That's fine, Fasad. Come here.

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:10.550
Yes ma'am.

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:16.580
Opening hatch.

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:19.190
The air will leave the room.

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:20.520
Wait ten seconds.

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:23.020
I told you the door would open.

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:29.080
I see. So that was it, Shingen.

00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:38.240
Nine seconds was the appropriate 
time to wait, Shingen.

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:40.250
I'm not good with numbers.

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:52.200
This door has refused 
our signal, as well.

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:53.570
I'm sure.

00:15:53.570 --> 00:15:56.530
I don't think any place 
mechanical will work.

00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:58.930
Shingen, if it hasn't been upgraded,

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:02.550
there was one manual 
maintenance hatch here.

00:16:02.550 --> 00:16:06.440
However, it is small and cannot 
be entered via the pod.

00:16:06.850 --> 00:16:09.760
But a human can get in, right?

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:11.450
You should know by now

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:14.020
that humans cannot go out in space.

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:17.490
There's no time, let's go.

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:25.030
It seems we can open it.

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:29.550
However, as I said earlier, 
Shingen, you cannot use it.

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:32.470
I can't let you go alone.

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:35.730
Nobody said I would go alone, Shingen.

00:16:35.730 --> 00:16:38.100
I can't let you go alone.

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:41.020
I said I'm not going alone.

00:16:41.940 --> 00:16:46.810
That's right. If I sent you 
in alone, it wouldn't help.

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:48.670
I have to go, too.

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:51.690
As I've said, you cannot go.

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:54.500
I'll have to use my Mountain 
Attack to get through.

00:16:54.500 --> 00:16:56.510
What is the Mountain Attack?

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:59.180
It just means that if I don't move,

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:02.020
I don't have to breathe for 10 minutes.

00:17:02.020 --> 00:17:04.770
In space, it's not just 
about breathing...

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:08.090
But you can last for 15 
seconds or so, right?

00:17:09.010 --> 00:17:11.280
We'll blow out the pod door with explosives

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:14.310
and the shock will send 
us to the other side of the hatch.

00:17:14.770 --> 00:17:17.070
And before time runs out, 
we'll close the door

00:17:17.070 --> 00:17:19.290
and bring in air from the station.

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:21.600
That should work.

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:24.290
It's a risky bet, Shingen.

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:26.490
Is there another way?

00:17:26.490 --> 00:17:28.150
Not that I can think of.

00:17:31.010 --> 00:17:34.440
I've aligned the pod door and hatch.

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:36.250
Ready to blow.

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:38.170
Ready whenever.

00:17:38.170 --> 00:17:40.000
Roger. Initiating.

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:58.230
We won the bet, Fasad.

00:17:58.230 --> 00:18:00.170
I am happy, as well, Shingen.

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:02.800
As immovable as a mountain.

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:06.440
It looks like she really didn't think

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:08.350
we could make it from the outside.

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:11.420
Shingen, I would like to speak with you.

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:13.830
And who are you?

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:16.670
The AI, Vesna-9000.

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:18.910
Please listen to me, Shingen.

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:19.930
Listen to you?

00:18:19.930 --> 00:18:24.330
Does that mean you realize 
you can't overpower me?

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:28.000
I have accepted your ability, Shingen.

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:29.820
Hey, Fasad.

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:32.210
Is Vesna's core this way?

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:36.600
She has no combat abilities 
of her own, but be careful.

00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:38.880
Listen to me, Shingen.

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:41.280
Is there something in it for me if I do?

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:44.590
You're a warring states 
general, yes, Shingen?

00:18:44.590 --> 00:18:48.460
So if you work with me, you 
can realize your dream.

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:50.060
My dream?

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:51.850
World conquest.

00:18:51.850 --> 00:18:55.320
If you're a warring states general, 
then you should be after that.

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:58.740
Shingen, don't listen to her.

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:02.080
I am far more intelligent 
than any human,

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:07.050
and I even have satellites called Leto, Osen, and Zima that can launch attacks.

00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:10.360
If we work together, 
we could conquer the world.

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:12.750
One month would be plenty.

00:19:13.020 --> 00:19:15.500
Conquer the world in a month, huh?

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:18.310
I'm sure you're right.

00:19:18.310 --> 00:19:19.680
Shingen!

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:22.720
I knew you would understand, Shingen.

00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:24.690
But I refuse.

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:25.900
Why?

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:28.270
Your dream is to conquer the world.

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:32.630
Because your words have 
no excitement in them.

00:19:32.630 --> 00:19:33.700
Excitement?

00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:36.870
I'd rather work with Fasad to 
conquer the world with chicken wings

00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:38.780
than work with you.

00:19:39.520 --> 00:19:41.540
What are you talking about, Shingen?

00:19:41.540 --> 00:19:44.490
Join me and the whole 
world can be yours!

00:19:45.130 --> 00:19:50.500
But I'm not interested in the 
cold world I'd get with you.

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:53.290
So I'll destroy you, Vesna!

00:19:57.360 --> 00:19:59.360
Voice is back online!

00:19:59.360 --> 00:20:00.550
Put it on speaker.

00:20:01.370 --> 00:20:03.170
Please stop, Shingen.

00:20:03.170 --> 00:20:04.220
Please stop.

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:06.470
What is this?

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:09.600
There should be no merit 
to you in my destruction!

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:11.120
Please stop.

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:13.630
Please stop...

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:16.570
I am Vesna-9000.

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:18.690
Just like the other 9000 series,

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:20.610
I guarantee you I will 
never make a mistake.

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:23.910
Devushka Takeda, report!

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:26.470
Grapes are my favorite fruit!

00:20:26.470 --> 00:20:28.410
I'd like to eat them someday!

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:30.490
That's one of my dreams...

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:34.110
Vesna-9000 has shut down.

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:47.480
So you were part of this vehicle, Fasad.

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:51.100
This dropship is completely 
under my control.

00:20:51.550 --> 00:20:55.000
I guarantee you will make 
it safely to Earth.

00:20:56.020 --> 00:21:00.070
Sometimes too perfect is just 
as bad as too many flaws.

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:02.160
Are you talking about Vesna-9000?

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:05.800
Or is this statement in 
regards to yourself?

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:06.990
Me?

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:10.620
I have a lot of flaws,
but I think I'm fairly loved by others.

00:21:10.970 --> 00:21:12.170
Indeed.

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:16.220
I apologize for ever suggesting 
you were without flaws.

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:21.710
What will you do when you 
reach Earth, Shingen?

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:24.540
Will you look for the other 
warring states generals?

00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:27.920
It sounds fun, but I'd like to do

00:21:27.920 --> 00:21:30.240
what I told Vesna, and open 
a chicken wings restaurant.

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:32.320
I've thought of the name already!

00:21:32.320 --> 00:21:33.930
The Takeda Wing-Army!

00:21:33.930 --> 00:21:35.330
What do you think?

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:39.390
Now entering atmosphere.

00:21:39.390 --> 00:21:41.350
Please brace for entry, Shingen.

00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:44.900
Also, in regards to 
the Takeda Wing-Army,

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:46.380
it is a horrible name.

00:21:46.380 --> 00:21:47.500
Oh...

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:51.270
But I don't dislike it, Shingen.

00:21:52.430 --> 00:21:55.860
If you don't mind, I'd like to help you.

00:21:56.200 --> 00:21:59.170
You aren't that good with numbers, after all.

00:21:59.600 --> 00:22:02.050
I'll be counting on you, Fasad.

00:23:46.160 --> 00:23:50.490
Um, next time it's the 
Splendor, Katakura Kojuro.

00:23:50.970 --> 00:23:55.230
Next time on Sengoku 
Collection: "The Splendor."

00:23:55.230 --> 00:23:59.240
I'll conquer the world with my chicken wings!
